{#- Home hero (#inicio): the lab's fingerprint mark rebuilt live as a small neural network.
    css/pages/hero.css + js/hero.js (both linked by index.njk).
    - The visual comes first in the DOM, as it is seen on phones (hero.css places it in the right column from
      960px and on landscape screens).
    - <path data-hero-source> is what hero.js samples: keep its d and the <g transform> identical to public/favicon.svg.
    - The visible still (no JS, no canvas, any error) is a frame of that network: #hero-ridges are its seeded chains
      as polylines and .hero__minutiae its ridge endings (ring + direction tick), exported once from hero.js's
      pipeline (rasterise, sample, connect; budget 480) in a scratch copy. Re-export them if the mark changes.
    - [data-hero-avoid] caps the animation's alpha behind the text block.
    - " · " separators get a no-break space before the dot (the text is escaped first), so a wrapped line never
      starts with it.
    - The print is decorative (aria-hidden). -#}
